---
pagination:
  data: redirects
  size: 1
  alias: r
redirects:
  - { from: "/schedule/", to: "/program/" }
  - { from: "/accessibility/", to: "/join/#interpretation", hashes: { "espanol": "/es/join/#interpretation", "etiquette": "/join/#etiquette", "other": "/join/#accessibility" } }
  - { from: "/meeting/", to: "/principles/" }
  - { from: "/poster/", to: "/flyer/#printable-poster" }
  - { from: "/es/poster/", to: "/es/flyer/#printable-poster", lang: "es" }
permalink: "{{ r.from }}"
layout: false
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- Pages that moved in the October 2026 redesign, and the printable poster, which joined the flyer page
    (#printable-poster) in a later round. GitHub Pages has no server-side redirects, so each
    old address is a tiny page that forwards at once and names the new page as its canonical, so search
    engines move the old address over (no noindex, which would contradict the canonical; the stubs are
    already left out of the sitemap). Links into sections of the old one-page home (/#join, /es/#unirse …)
    can't be redirected by the server either; partials/head.njk sends those on with a small script.
    `hashes` (optional): where the old page's #sections go (/accessibility/#espanol → the Spanish join
    page). A small script, run before the meta refresh, forwards them; any other #fragment, or no
    JavaScript, goes to `to`. `lang` (optional, default en): the language of the stub's one line. -#}
{%- set rEs = r.lang == "es" -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ 'es' if rEs else 'en' }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ site.name }}</title>
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ r.to | absUrl }}">
{% if r.hashes %}<script>(function(){var m={{ r.hashes | dump | safe }},h=location.hash.slice(1);if(h&&Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(m,h))location.replace(m[h])})()</script>{% endif %}
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ r.to }}">
</head>
<body>
<p>{{ "Esta página cambió de lugar:" if rEs else "This page has moved:" }} <a href="{{ r.to }}">{{ r.to | absUrl }}</a></p>
</body>
</html>
